                <pb facs="0113" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.01/2062: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Algiers</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-26T00:00:00-04:00">April 26,
                            1943—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>800. For Murphy. As suggested in final paragraph your 662, April 20, you may
                    endeavor informally to confirm your interpretation of certain points in the
                    Giraud Memorandum. You should not, of course, express any views on the
                    subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
